<p><em>Retrieving individual pages is not supported with this file type. Re=
questing `</em>/*<code>(or omitting Accept header) and page 1 will return t=
he entire document as a single file. Any other page number will result in</=
code>404 Not Found`.</p>
<p><a name=3D"how-to-use"></a></p>
<h2 id=3D"how-to-use">How to Use</h2>
<p><a name=3D"head-request"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"head-request">HEAD Request</h3>
<p>The <code>HEAD</code> Request can be used to get information about the c=
ontent before getting actual content bytes. This can be useful for getting =
the number of pages (must include the <code>pages</code> query parameter), =
previewing the negotiated content type, and previewing the content length. =
If the pages query parameter is included in the request, <code>Hyland-Item-=
Count</code> header will be included on the response.</p>
<p><a name=3D"without-page-query"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"without-page-query-parameter">Without Page Query Parameter</h4>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">HEAD</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/1/renditions/2/content</span> =
HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: image/tiff</code></pre><pre c=
lass=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> OK
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: {bytes length}
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: image/tiff</code></pre>=
<p><a name=3D"with-page-query"></a></p>
<h4 id=3D"with-page-query-parameter">With Page Query Parameter</h4>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">HEAD</span> <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/1/renditions/2/content?pages=
=3D1</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: image/tiff</code></pre><pre c=
lass=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> OK
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: {bytes length}
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: image/tiff
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Hyland-Item-Count</span>: 3</code></pre><p><=
a name=3D"retrieving-entire-document"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"retrieving-entire-document">Retrieving Entire Document</h3>
<p>The best approach is to use <code>latest</code> for the revision ID and =
<code>default</code> for the file type ID unless a specific revision or ren=
dition is known to be needed. If you simply want to retrieve the document a=
s a single file, specifying a default media type and no pages is the best a=
pproach, as a document will be returned successfully every time.</p>
<p>This example shows the best approach:</p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GET</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/latest/renditions/default/conte=
nt</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: */*</code></pre><pre class=3D=
"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> OK
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: {byte length}
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: image/tiff

<span class=3D"coffeescript">[bytes <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">for</span>=
 the entire <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">document</span>]</span></code></p=
re><p>This example shows how to specify a revision and rendition:</p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GET</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/1/renditions/2/content</span> H=
TTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: image/tiff</code></pre><pre c=
lass=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> OK
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: {bytes length}
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: image/tiff

<span class=3D"coffeescript">[bytes <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">for</span>=
 the entire <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">document</span>]</span></code></p=
re><p><a name=3D"retrieving-single-page"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"retrieving-single-page">Retrieving Single Page</h3>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GET</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/1/renditions/2/content?pages=3D=
2</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: image/tiff</code></pre><pre c=
lass=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> OK
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: {bytes length}
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: image/tiff
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Hyland-Item-Count</span>: 3

<span class=3D"coffeescript">[bytes <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">for</span>=
 the <span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>nd page <span class=3D"hljs-keywor=
d">of</span> the <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">document</span>]</span></cod=
e></pre><p><a name=3D"nonexistent-page"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"requesting-a-page-that-does-not-exist">Requesting a Page that doe=
s not Exist</h3>
<p>This example document has 3 pages, so the request below will return <cod=
e>404 Not Found</code>.</p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GET</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/latest/renditions/default/conte=
nt?pages=3D4</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: image/tiff</code></pre><pre c=
lass=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">404</span> Not Fou=
nd
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: application/problem+jso=
n

<span class=3D"json">{
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"title"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-string">"=
Not Found"</span>,
    <span class=3D"hljs-attr">"status"</span>: <span class=3D"hljs-number">=
404</span>
}</span></code></pre><p><a name=3D"retrieving-byte-range-without-an-etag"><=
/a></p>
<h3 id=3D"retrieving-byte-range-without-an-etag">Retrieving Byte Range with=
out an ETag</h3>
<p>Initially, you will not have an ETag for the document. One will be retur=
ned after the first=20
request though.</p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GET</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/1/renditions/2/content</span> H=
TTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: image/tiff
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Range</span>: bytes=3D0-999</code></pre><pre=
 class=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> OK
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: 1000
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: image/tiff
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Range</span>: 0-999/9000
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept-Ranges</span>: bytes
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">ETag</span>: qwertyuiop

<span class=3D"applescript">[<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">first</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-number">1000</span> bytes <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">of</=
span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">the</span> document]</span></code></pre>=
<p>Notice that the total number of bytes is also included in the <code>Cont=
ent-Range</code> header. This can=20
be used to determine the number of requests that must be made to retrieve t=
he entire document.</p>
<p><a name=3D"retrieving-byte-range-with-an-etag"></a></p>
<h3 id=3D"retrieving-byte-range-with-an-etag">Retrieving Byte Range with an=
 ETag</h3>
<p>After your first request, you'll have an ETag that you can include on su=
bsequent requests. This=20
ETag is important to ensure that the bytes you are retrieving are always fr=
om the exact same=20
rendering of the document. If you do not include this ETag on other request=
s, the document will=20
be re-rendered and there's a possibility the rendering could be slightly di=
fferent. </p>
<pre class=3D"hljs"><code><span class=3D"hljs-keyword">GET</span> <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-string">/documents/101/revisions/latest/renditions/default/conte=
nt</span> HTTP/1.1
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Authorization</span>: Bearer valid-token
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept</span>: image/tiff
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Range</span>: bytes=3D1000-1999
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">If-Match</span>: qwertyuiop</code></pre><pre=
 class=3D"hljs"><code>HTTP/1.1 <span class=3D"hljs-number">200</span> OK
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Length</span>: 1000
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Type</span>: image/tiff
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Content-Range</span>: 1000-1999/9000
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">Accept-Ranges</span>: bytes
<span class=3D"hljs-attribute">ETag</span>: qwertyuiop

<span class=3D"applescript">[<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">second</span> <sp=
an class=3D"hljs-number">1000</span> bytes <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">of<=
/span> <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">the</span> document]</span></code></pre=
